# L §5.16: cdf, pdf, pmf "take a distribution value, a random fact read directly, or an affine form of one";
# "the transformed function of D (pdf divided by |a|)".  uniform(0, 4): pdf 1/4 (exact, table); pdf(2 × X, 2) =
# pdf(D, 1)/2 = 0.125; cdf(-X, -1) = P(X >= 1) = 3/4.  cdf of normal(0, 1) at 0 is Φ(0) = 1/2, detected exactly
# (L §7.3).  binomial(4, 1/2): pmf(0) = 1/16, cdf(1) = 5/16, exact.  "An ask that reaches crps or pdf states orient
# lower or orient higher", and orient is printed (L §5.15).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input z: dist
input u01: dist
input u4: dist
input cnt: dist
input q25: num
input two: num
input lvl: num
def pdf1: num = pdf(u4, 1) at reader
def pdf2: num = pdf(two * u4, two) at reader
def cdf1: num = cdf(-u4, -1) at reader
def cdfz: num = cdf(z, 0) to 1e-9 at reader
def pm: num = pmf(cnt, 0) at reader
def cb: num = cdf(cnt, 1) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  z = normal(0, 1) to 1e-9
  u01 = uniform(0, 1) to 0.001
  u4 = uniform(0, 4) to 0.001
  cnt = binomial(4, 0.5)
  q25 = 0.25
  two = 2
  lvl = 0.5

ask d1: pdf1, pdf2 law 2026-06-30 orient higher
ask d2: cdf1, cdfz, pm, cb law 2026-06-30
=== expect
d1: (0.25, 0.125)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
  orient higher
d2: (0.75, 0.5, 0.0625, 0.3125)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
